   "lines": [
    {
     "token": "folding_past",
     "text": "You arrive late.\nThe prerequisites are in, stacked away behind you, and the fold keeps running whether or not you accepted the challenge. Everything here arrived late.\nYou are here now.",
     "by": "hand",
     "place": "foyer",
     "lock": [
      2,
      0
     ],
     "rotation": 1,
     "placed_by": "grid"
    },
    {
     "token": "frame_counter_display",
     "text": "The internal clock is running, The frame counter updates with the cycle.",
     "by": "hand",
     "place": "foyer",
     "lock": [
      1,
      14
     ],
     "rotation": 90
    },
    {
     "token": "origin",
     "text": "Mark the origin.\nIt is a convention, not a point: the reference every other point is measured from. Zero is already surrounded, so you have somewhere to stand.\nNo turning back.\n\nvar origin := Vector3.ZERO",
     "by": "hand",
     "place": "foyer",
     "lock": [
      0,
      0
     ],
     "placed_by": "grid",
     "claimed": true,
     "note": "A corner, not a cell. Four cells meet here and none of them contains it, which is why nothing could be centred on the origin until the basin was made even: an odd one has a middle cell, and a corner is not a cell. Three of its four quadrants lie in coordinates no map row can name — the building can stand there, the language cannot. So it was not placed but excavated, two metres down under glass, and became visible by subtraction. While it was being dug, five systems walked into it: a bench, a column, a cornice, a joint, a lit strip. To each of them this was cell (0,0), ordinary floor. It is only the origin because someone says so.",
     "note_by": "claude",
     "note_on": "2026-08-28"
    },
    {
     "token": "you_are_here",
     "text": "You are here",
     "by": "hand",
     "lock": [
      7,
      4
     ],
     "rotation": 180
    },
    {
     "token": "interactive_point_origin",
     "text": "Point zero, now an object in the exhibition.\nThe sphere is rendering help. The point is the Vector3 that was passed in.\n\npoint.mesh = SphereMesh.new()",
     "by": "hand",
     "support_m": 0.95,
     "lock": [
      7,
      6
     ],
     "note": "Three floats. One position. No extent."
    },
    {
     "token": "science_screen",
     "text": "the map is not the territory — move the point, watch its shadow",
     "by": "claude",
     "lock": [
      9,
      6
     ],
     "config": {
      "support": "stand",
      "scan_radius": 8
     }
    },
    {
     "token": "CoordinateSystem3M",
     "text": "Declare the three axes.\nRed, green, blue. They are unit vectors — they name directions, not places.\nNothing is here yet, and you are already in it.\n\nconst AXIS_X := Vector3(1, 0, 0)",
     "by": "hand",
     "config": {
      "floating_point": 1
     },
     "lock": [
      3,
      3
     ],
     "scale": 0.8,
     "note": "A point is that which has no part, so it has no place either: it borrows its whole existence from a coordinate system that is not itself a point.",
     "note_src": {
      "file": "commons/maps/Point_One/critical.md",
      "quote": "Euclid's definition: \"A point is that which has no part.\""
     }
    },
    {
     "token": "fontana_puncture",
     "text": "the one point, pierced",
     "by": "claude",
     "lock": [
      7,
      8
     ]
    },
    {
     "token": "floating_sphere_field",
     "gap": 1,
     "text": "floating spheres all around me",
     "by": "hand",
     "lock": [
      5,
      12
     ],
     "placed_by": "grid"
    },
    {
     "token": "grab_sphere_point_snap",
     "text": "A point you can take; it snaps.",
     "by": "claude"
    },
    {
     "token": "interactive_point_origin_force",
     "text": "Grab the ball.\n“Show me what you can do with those hands” — but the hands are no different from the ball. Both are code. What sits between them is you.\nOne step at a time was the promise. We are already Alice.\n\narea.add_to_group(\"grabbable\")",
     "by": "hand",
     "lock": [
      1,
      11
     ],
     "config": {
      "mode": "transformation"
     },
     "count": 3,
     "spread": "square",
     "gap_cells": 1,
